.SH SHELL SYNTAX
.SS Commands and Operators
Simple commands, pipelines using
.BR | ,
and logical operators
.BR && ,
.BR || ,
.BR ; ,
and
.B !
are supported.
.SS Redirects
.TP
.IR "> " and " >>"
Redirect stdout; append with
.BR >> .
.TP
.I <
Redirect stdin.
.TP
.I 2>
Redirect stderr.
.TP
.I &>
Redirect both stdout and stderr.
.TP
.I <<<
Here string.
.TP
.IR "<< " and " <<\-"
Here document; the
.B <<\-
variant strips leading tabs.
.TP
.IR "<& " and " >&"
Duplicate file descriptors.
.TP
.IR ">>& " and " >|"
Append to file descriptor; overwrite with
.BR >| .
.SS Variable Expansion
.TP
.I ${var:\-default}
Use
.I default
if
.I var
is unset or empty.
.TP
.I ${var:+alt}
Use
.I alt
if
.I var
is set and non-empty.
.TP
.I ${var:=val}
Assign
.I val
to
.I var
if unset or empty, then expand.
.TP
.I ${var?err}
Display
.I err
and exit if
.I var
is unset or empty.
.TP
.I ${#var}
Length of
.IR var .
.TP
.IR ${var#} ", " ${var##}
Remove shortest or longest prefix matching a pattern.
.TP
.IR ${var%} ", " ${var%%}
Remove shortest or longest suffix matching a pattern.
.TP
.IR ${var/old/new} ", " ${var//old/new}
Replace the first or all occurrences of
.I old
with
.IR new .
.SS Parameter Expansion Extras
.TP
.I ${var@Q}
Quoted value.
.TP
.I ${var@E}
Expanded value with escape processing.
.TP
.I ${var@U}
Uppercase expansion.
.TP
.I ${var@u}
Capitalize the first character.
.TP
.I ${var@a}
Attribute flags of the variable.
.TP
.I ${var@P}
Prompt-expansion of the value.
.SS Other Expansions
.TP
.I $()
Command substitution (also backtick syntax).
.TP
.IR $(( )) " and " $[ ]
Arithmetic expansion.
.TP
.I {a,b,c}
Brace expansion; also ranges like
.IR {1..5} .
.TP
.IR ~ " and " ~user
Tilde expansion to home directories.
.TP
.IR <() " and " >()
Process substitution.
.TP
.I $'...'
ANSI-C quoting with escape sequences.
.TP
.I <<
Here documents.
.TP
.I <<<
Here strings.
