.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1\-125
Non-zero failure (command-specific).
.TP
.B 126
Command found but not executable.
.TP
.B 127
Command not found.
.TP
.B 128+N
Terminated by signal
.IR N .
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGINT
.RB ( ^C )
and
.B SIGQUIT
.RB ( ^\e )
are caught in interactive mode to interrupt or quit the current foreground
process.
.B SIGTERM
is handled gracefully, allowing cleanup of temporary files and history.
.B SIGHUP
is forwarded to background jobs when the shell exits.
.B SIGTSTP
.RB ( ^Z )
suspends the foreground job and
.B SIGCONT
resumes it.
.B SIGWINCH
updates internal terminal dimensions on resize.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.I ctx \-c "echo hello"
Execute a single command and exit.
.TP
.I ctx \-f script.sh
Run a shell script.
.TP
.I ctx \-p
Start in POSIX mode for maximum portability.
.TP
.I ctx \-i \-T '%n@%h %w> '
Start an interactive session with a custom prompt.
.TP
.I ctx \-\-benchmark \-c "sleep 0.1"
Run a command in benchmark mode to measure performance.
